**Corollary 6.5 (exact post-update image on the full balanced slice).** As $t$
ranges over $\mathcal B_s$, the current boundary $q_H(\rho t)$ has exactly
$2s+1$ values, indexed by
$k_1\in\{-2s,-2s+2,\ldots,2s\}$. This is a coarser partition than the initial
two-window boundary. The family in Theorem 6.4 retains the stronger requirement
that the entire initial boundary is already common.

Proof. The current boundary is $(0,E_1,6s)$. Formula (DAF.15) makes its phase
a function of $k_1$, and (DAF.13) realizes every displayed sum $P+Q$. Normal-form
uniqueness separates these sums. Initial pairs with the same sum can have
different $k_0$, so the post-update image alone must not be substituted for a
common supplied initial boundary in Theorem 6.4.

